<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  coop_rviz.launch
  ================
  RViz for the cooperation, on its own.

    roslaunch uav_scout_bushfire coop_rviz.launch

  Attaches to an incident that is already running. Nothing here publishes to the
  scenario - it subscribes and draws - so it can be started, killed and started
  again at any point in a run without disturbing Gazebo, the planners or the
  fleets. That is the point of it being a separate file: the world takes the
  longest to load and is the thing you least want to restart.

  bushfire_coop.launch includes this when rviz:=true, so there is one definition
  of what the view is rather than two that drift.

  What to look at
  ===============
  Fire as obstacles   the fire_costmap cloud. This is the display that answers
                      "why did a tender drive through that fire" - if it is
                      missing or in the wrong place, move_base is blind to fire.
  scout_N plan        each tender's live route round the timber and the fires.
  Shared map          the occupancy grid both Scouts plan on.

  The aircraft scans are off by default. Three more planes of dots over the same
  trunks makes the picture harder to read, not easier; tick them on when the
  question is about what a drone can see.
-->
<launch>

  <arg name="rviz_config" default="$(find uav_scout_bushfire)/rviz/coop.rviz" />
  <arg name="delay" default="0"
       doc="bushfire_coop.launch waits for the world; started by hand, do not" />

  <!-- Join the two TF trees, so one RViz can show the whole incident.
       The aircraft are published under `world` (Gazebo ground truth) and the
       Scouts under `map` (the navigation stack), and nothing else connects
       them - so RViz in `world` draws the drones and no scouts, and in `map`
       the reverse, with the map, costmaps and plans visible in neither.

       Identity, and correctly so: the map was generated from this world with
       its origin field placing the image corner at (-10.6, -10.6), which puts
       the map frame's origin on the arena centre, where the world origin is.
       The residual difference is the Scouts' odometry drift, measured at about
       0.28 m after several minutes of driving - which is what AMCL would
       correct if this used it, and is why this is published rather than
       assumed.

       It lives here rather than in bushfire_coop.launch because it exists for
       the benefit of the view: nothing in the scenario looks it up. -->
  <node pkg="tf2_ros" type="static_transform_publisher" name="world_to_map"
        args="0 0 0 0 0 0 world map" />

  <node name="rviz" pkg="rviz" type="rviz" args="-d $(arg rviz_config)"
        output="screen" required="false"
        launch-prefix="bash -c 'sleep $(arg delay) &amp;&amp; exec &quot;$0&quot; &quot;$@&quot;' --" />

</launch>
